§§ `For the owner or occupier: a notice to remove graffiti (s 18)`

-- The situations (D8, as corrected): from "Must I have the graffiti obliterated" to s 24, each question takes the
-- notice second, straight after the role. With no notice it does not arise and nothing after the notice is asked.
-- Consent is not a situation for these questions: only "Must I have the graffiti obliterated" asks it, after the
-- notice, as before D8. So the cases below with a notice given hold whether or not the owner or occupier says there
-- was consent; the section "a notice given for graffiti said to be put up without consent" asks every one of them on
-- one set of facts. The six questions of an affected person's own times (ss 22, 23) also do not arise for an occupier
-- whose landlord was given the notice (s 20), and nothing after the notice is asked.

-- Can the local government require me to obliterate it (s 18(1), (2))? A mural I commissioned, seen from the street,
-- that the council finds offensive: yes. Seen only from my back yard: no. Tagged without my consent: no (s 25 instead),
-- the answer at law rather than `does not arise`, with nothing else asked (asserted in the section on a notice given for
-- graffiti said to be put up without consent).
#ASSERT `Can the local government require me to have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the local government require me to have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` TRUE FALSE `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the local government require me to have the graffiti obliterated` `as the accused` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Can the local government require me to have the graffiti obliterated` `as the seller` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Must I obliterate it (s 18)? The notice was given to me: yes. It was given to my tenant (the occupier): not me, and
-- nothing else is asked. Given to me, but not visible from a public place: no. Given to me for graffiti put up without
-- consent: no (s 18(1)(a)), asserted with the other notice questions on those facts below. No notice: does not arise.
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `given to my occupier, I own` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I occupy` TRUE FALSE `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `no notice` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the accused` `an unasked notice position` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the seller` `an unasked notice position` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- By when (s 18(2))? Notice of 1 March 2027 allowing 14 days: by 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By what date must the graffiti be obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own` `1 March 2027` 14 EQUALS `by` `15 March 2027`
#ASSERT `By what date must the graffiti be obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `no notice` `an unasked date` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `By what date must the graffiti be obliterated` `as the accused` `an unasked notice position` `an unasked date` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `By what date must the graffiti be obliterated` `as the seller` `an unasked notice position` `an unasked date` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

