§§ `For the owner or occupier: a notice given for graffiti said to be put up without consent (the D8 correction)`

-- Before the correction, an owner or occupier who answered that the graffiti was put up without consent was told that
-- every notice question after the first did not arise, the deadlines to dispute the notice among them. Now the notice
-- is the situation, and consent is asked only where it changes the answer. On one set of facts: I bought a house and
-- live in it; the seller had commissioned a mural on the front wall, and I say it was put up without consent. On
-- 1 March 2027 the council gives me a notice allowing 14 days. Asked on 20 March 2027, having done nothing:
-- - the council cannot require it of me (s 18(1)(a)), and on my account I need not obliterate it: no, and no;
-- - but the notice's date was 15 March; it was not complied with in time; the most fine so far is $5 000 + 5 x $500 =
--   $7 500, with $500 for each further day; the owner need not be told (I am the owner); the council may obliterate it
--   and recover its cost from me; I own and occupy, so no one can be ordered to pay me back;
-- - I must be given written reasons; I may object now, by 30 March (the 28th day, 29 March, is Easter Monday); the
--   objection is still open until then; the council may allow further time; I may apply to the Tribunal now, by
--   12 April; that is still open until then; the Tribunal may extend it; and if I object, the notice is suspended.
-- Whether there was consent is what an objection or a review would decide (ss 22, 23). Only "Must I have the graffiti
-- obliterated" reads consent; the others do not take it, so these answers hold whether or not there was consent.
#ASSERT `Can the local government require me to have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I have the graffiti obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `By what date must the graffiti be obliterated` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` `1 March 2027` 14 EQUALS `by` `15 March 2027`
#ASSERT `Has the notice been complied with in time` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` `1 March 2027` 14 FALSE `an unasked date` `20 March 2027` EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not complying with the notice` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` `1 March 2027` 14 FALSE `an unasked date` `20 March 2027` FALSE EQUALS amount 7500
#ASSERT `How much is the further fine for each day the notice is not complied with` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` EQUALS amount 500
#ASSERT `Must the owner be told in writing that the notice was given` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `What may the local government do if the notice is not complied with` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` FALSE `1 March 2027` 14 `20 March 2027` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `obliterate the graffiti, and recover its reasonable cost from you as a debt`
#ASSERT `Can I get some of what the notice cost me back from the owner or occupier` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` TRUE EQUALS `no one: you both own and occupy the property`
#ASSERT `Must I be given written reasons for the notice and told of my rights` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I object to the notice` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` FALSE `1 March 2027` 0 `20 March 2027` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `By what date must I lodge my objection` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` `1 March 2027` 0 EQUALS `by` `30 March 2027`
#ASSERT `Did I lodge my objection in time` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` `1 March 2027` 0 FALSE `an unasked date` `20 March 2027` EQUALS `still open until` `30 March 2027`
#ASSERT `Can the local government still allow me further time to object` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal for a review now` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` `1 March 2027` FALSE `an unasked date` `an unasked fact` `an unasked date` `20 March 2027` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `By what date must I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` FALSE `1 March 2027` `an unasked date` `an unasked fact` `an unasked date` `20 March 2027` EQUALS `by` `12 April 2027`
#ASSERT `Did I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal in time` `as the owner or occupier` `given to me, I own and occupy` FALSE `1 March 2027` `an unasked date` `an unasked fact` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` FALSE `an unasked date` `20 March 2027` EQUALS `still open until` `12 April 2027`
