-- s 12: a volunteer hurt on my property removing graffiti. I own it: no action against me unless gross negligence. I
-- rent it from a private landlord, so I am an occupier but not an owner (LG Act s 1.4): s 12 does not protect me, and
-- gross negligence is not asked. No graffiti removal work on my property: does not arise, nothing else asked.
#ASSERT `Can I be sued if someone is hurt removing graffiti on my property` `as the owner or occupier` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: as the owner, an action in tort does not lie against you; it may be taken against the State instead`
#ASSERT `Can I be sued if someone is hurt removing graffiti on my property` `as the owner or occupier` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: your breach of your duty of care would amount to gross negligence, which s 12 does not protect`
#ASSERT `Can I be sued if someone is hurt removing graffiti on my property` `as the owner or occupier` TRUE FALSE `an unasked fact` EQUALS `s 12 does not protect you: it protects only the owner of the place, not an occupier who is not its owner`
#ASSERT `Can I be sued if someone is hurt removing graffiti on my property` `as the owner or occupier` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Can I be sued if someone is hurt removing graffiti on my property` `as the accused` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Can I be sued if someone is hurt removing graffiti on my property` `as the seller` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
